ned expand empty tables\" [Page 1/4 (showing 1-5)]:\n\n> 💡 **Next page**: `ki_search(query=\"Table ratio calculation flexible columns collapse zero width ratio distribution constrained expand empty tables\", page=2)` (or `offset=5`)\n\n1. [KI] **ADR-0004: Ratio Distribution & Column Allocation** (`.ki-base/decisions/0004-ratio-distribution-and-layout.md`, score: 18.219)\n   > # ADR-0004: Ratio Distribution & Column Allocation - **Status:** Accepted - **Date:** 2026-11-08 - **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers ## Context When...\n2. [KI] **ADR-0004: Ratio Distribution & Column Allocation** (`.ki-base/decisions/0004-ratio-distribution-and-layout.md`, score: 18.219)\n   > # ADR-0004: Ratio Distribution & Column Allocation - **Status:** Accepted - **Date:** 2026-11-08 - **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers ## Context When...\n3. [KI] **KI: Rich Core (Syntax, Tables, Text & Tracebacks)** (`.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_syntax.md`, score: 17.991)\n   > <!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 --> # KI: Rich Core (Syntax, Tables, Text & Tracebacks) ## Overview Implements high-level data presentation components: `Table` (grid formatting with auto-wrapping), `Text` (styled...\n4. [KI] **KI: Rich Core (Internal Utilities & Platform Adaptors)** (`.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_null.md`, score: 11.748)\n   > ...Overview Provides internal mathematical routines, layout ratio solvers, text wrapping primitives, platform Win32 console structures, and base ABC protocols. It forms the low-level foundation for rendering...\n5. [KI] **KI: Rich Core (Console, Alignment & Core Layouts)** (`.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_align.md`, score: 7.572)\n   > ...`Console` class, ANSI escape sequence decoder, cell width calculators, border box constants, and alignment/column containers. It coordinates measurement, rendering, and terminal stream emission. ## Entry Points...\n\n*Showing 5 of 18 results. Call `ki_search(query='Table ratio calculation flexible columns collapse zero width ratio distribution constrained expand empty tables', page=2)` (or `offset=5`) to view more.*"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_search"},"isError":false,"durationMs":68,"timestamp":1794168853027},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_7wRycaqDhcJ2YxzWf6TApaRv","name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","arguments":{"rel_path":".ki-base/decisions/0004-ratio-distribution-and-layout.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_QsGG6ReOpd21Ai6NavEpM7zG","name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","arguments":{"rel_path":".ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_syntax.md","section":"Table"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":3,"output":92,"cacheRead":4966,"cacheWrite":627,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":5688,"cost":{"input":6.000000000000001e-7,"output":0.0001104,"cacheRead":0.00009932,"cacheWrite":0.00015675,"total":0.00036707,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794168853035,"responseId":"gen-1794168853-T7U5tNZtBsslISsZ7ROm","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":1779,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_7wRycaqDhcJ2YxzWf6TApaRv","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0004: Ratio Distribution & Column Allocation\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nWhen rendering tables and multi-pane split layouts, columns and panels have competing size constraints: minimum width, maximum width, fixed cell counts, or proportional ratios (`ratio=1`, `ratio=2`). In collapsed views or deeply nested tables, total available space can shrink to zero or negative values, risking `ZeroDivisionError` or layout breakage.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Two-Pass Space Resolution (`rich/_ratio.py`):**  \n   Space allocation via `ratio_resolve(total: int, edges: Sequence[Edge]) -> List[int]` must strictly adhere to the two-pass algorithm:\n   - **Pass 1 (Fixed & Minimum Constraints):** Allocate absolute minimum widths and fixed sizes first. Subtract allocated space from `total`.\n   - **Pass 2 (Proportional Ratios):** Distribute remaining space among flexible edges according to their `ratio` weights.\n2. **Boundary & Zero Protection Invariants:**\n   - If remaining space is zero or negative, flexible edges must receive `edge.minimum_size` (or 0) without performing division by total ratio weights.\n   - Algorithms must never raise `ZeroDivisionError` on zero-weight column sets; instead, distribute space evenly or fall back to minimum sizes.\n3. **Integer Conservation:**\n   - The sum of resolved column widths must never exceed `total` space allocated by the parent container. Fractional remainders are distributed deterministically across flexible columns.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Prevents crashes in nested or collapsed table views under narrow terminal dimensions.\n- Decouples table column layout logic from split-pane `Layout` mathematics.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":28,"timestamp":1794168854854},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_QsGG6ReOpd21Ai6NavEpM7zG","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# KI: Rich Core (Syntax, Tables, Text & Tracebacks)\n\n## Overview\nImplements high-level data presentation components: `Table` (grid formatting with auto-wrapping), `Text` (styled character spans), `Syntax` (Pygments code highlighting), `Traceback` (rich exception rendering), and `Tree` (hierarchical tree visualizations).\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n- `Table`: Flexible 2D data grid with borders, column wrapping, and header styling.\n- `Text`: Rich text container applying styles to string slices without markup overhead.\n- `Syntax`: Code syntax highlighter powered by Pygments themes with line numbers.\n- `Traceback`: Formatted exception hook and renderable for stack traces with syntax context.\n- `Tree`: Hierarchical outline/tree view with custom branch guides and leaf nodes.\n- `Theme`: Named style mapping defining cohesive terminal color palettes.\n\n## Key Components\n| Class / Function | File | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Table` | `rich/table.py` | Grid container managing column widths, padding, vertical alignment, and borders |\n| `Text` | `rich/text.py` | Span-based styled text representation supporting justification, wrapping, and highlights |\n| `Syntax` | `rich/syntax.py` | Lexes and styles source code across languages using Pygments lexers |\n| `Traceback` | `rich/traceback.py` | Exception traceback visualizer highlighting code context and local variables |\n| `Tree` | `rich/tree.py` | Recursive tree diagram builder with customizable guide lines |\n| `Theme` | `rich/theme.py` | Container mapping semantic style names to `Style` instances |\n| `TerminalTheme` | `rich/terminal_theme.py` | Terminal color scheme definitions (ANSI 16 colors + background + foreground) |\n\n## Testing & Verification\n- Test commands: `pytest tests/test_table.py tests/test_text.py tests/test_syntax.py tests/test_traceback.py tests/test_tree.py`\n- Test files: `tests/test_table.py`, `tests/test_text.py`, `tests/test_syntax.py`, `tests/test_traceback.py`, `tests/test_tree.py`\n\n## Non-obvious Details\n- **Table Width Solving in `rich/table.py` (L523–L585, ADR-0004)**:\n  - `Table._calculate_column_widths(self, console: Console, options: ConsoleOptions) -> List[int]` (L523): Computes column widths (including padding, excluding border `self._extra_width`).\n  - When `self.expand` is True and `columns` have `flexible` ratios (L535–L555), `flex_minimum` (L543) computes minimum widths for flexible columns (`max((column.min_width or 1) + get_padding_width(column._index), _range.minimum)`), and distributes `flexible_width = max(sum(flex_minimum), max_width - sum(fixed_widths))` via `ratio_distribute(flexible_width, ratios, flex_minimum)`.\n  - When `table_width > max_width` (L556–L575), `_collapse_widths` and `ratio_reduce` shrink columns, but must enforce `min_widths = [(column.min_width or 1) + get_padding_width(column._index) for column in columns]` so flexible columns never collapse to 0 width (`max_reduce = [max(0, w - min_w) for w, min_w in zip(widths, min_widths)]` and `widths = [max(min_w, _range.maximum or 0) ...]`).\n- **Traceback suppression flags**: Setting `_rich_traceback_omit = True` or `_rich_traceback_guard = True` inside a function's local scope conceals internal boilerplate frames during crashes.\n- **Text span arithmetic**: When slicing or joining `Text` objects, character index spans are adjusted or split automatically to preserve original formatting.\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n- **Table row modification during iteration**: Adding rows to a `Table` while rendering it concurrently will trigger size calculation mismatches.\n- **Traceback hook installation in libraries**: Calling `rich.traceback.install()` inside library code replaces global `sys.excepthook`, which can interfere with host application exception handling.\n\n\n## Related KIs\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/align.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/ansi.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/cells.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/columns.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/console.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/constrain.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/containers.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/control.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/default_styles.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/highlighter.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/jupyter.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/__init__.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/color.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/color_triplet.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/emoji.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]] (via `rich/_loop.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/markdown.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/markup.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/measure.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/padding.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/palette.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/panel.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/protocol.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/_pick.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/_ratio.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/_timer.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/_wrap.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/scope.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/segment.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/style.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/styled.py`)\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":36,"timestamp":1794168854857},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.encrypted\",\"data\":\"gAAAAABq8NgYZPvOM5SywpQyHbcbNOkOFKdQ_GbaRKKfMKnXYllC7W8FsWozA4b5C5OTn_UUM7l8EaDQkN3zkfd3J7GEoPCElxUpOsgrV8rrpVN1MeIUZXY96CVxYomJVel_e2YaFFS4j1GTNSX1NMi4x7ezYEmX4drWzcNghTEQPzSWfxPFfkj8U3PMKwDqFFbNvoOWiMN_1lUNNhGLIr0lyJJ_vwLrfHIv85fKHeLd2DfwwcTIsgDjS99Ood0jf-fXip2XMuQUaNjAOJslcNez_UPUFp8HvArhD80TkeIxhPC6hkEWOK-eyPTa7qZUQAijr6etJH1iSv0BhPtsBLCCNCnJfyEQZZRw9VNust6tL2WMpkOzroh92YpM-GtODxFO4uISTB7kcbv70TOa_hVpz1Uj0N1iFjX9GSlZ50T9meYFiOgT6c594TyaOmjsdw4tnmHLsF3LWjMwUVXzXgimEB1UnYqzja5SdKZWcHOndXcGVJn48fU-JzYmW3xvmTyniNrmOdxCtFnfo2e5bEmgSrg2jDhHMHSFyD-2QTeay2o3T9UKY5dPKNl_R3apAodLBNuG3-n5OzlbHWyzZCbWhSwM8um8U_0grDR1SALN_bftsNmVtO4tqfhPu7dBg2ToIvz4vDTucuqNvFLoUQLV3-N6gWdeO1BpGs8_1lpUxM9auJF9_sLsnAqciUOjUECqoe_fV8dI7R3pj1w8Qg9_DuJL6r9nF4aj98efn4dFrn6m_uCHSiYD4hsIxXTGFjfx18hoSsvlv6m1ISsKNEArIqb4Z4GW5ngnlxJC7AoLl_EOEYFpCZYaaLpZXw32tl6zE-ZHVJKIXwbucUMC_KM6-I73PkGqlE-4GFAoWJbUYyOla2tsMR4SIeuZsK-NVibd_Qb2Ib7gyNvG1ywkmUAT5oWVXtVhcaNDRbq9nkB59gjIxAWLpAacwlNbVKECSTRhOvESdx_Gdu-KsJOh45acA1WsryzwGGUNAn9a4O81iW_BD2XbqbG_L5P_HIDs-vAG8JFTqgKQFJU7lspVIsieMcYilYAmoENgWiwYv4zAmiVre5G2jieyCnnZ3vDhAgwbKUI69IJCZ-2mJ_XjyiqEjuYJ5EAfPR_aHkbniLwTvXM1eOJVnfkPc7YwLO74dhKm3t9TgUPiASFnT2DPdBj5SgTIDMTOFiVVfMLdn3KxjsokGdxIA9h4FOg58SCsjAZYw-URwDUR